Re: colors, you can see how the default colors are generated here:
http://phylo.wikidot.com/example-biogeobears-scripts#legends

Once you've used this to make "colors_list_for_states", then just add "colors_list_for_states= colors_list_for_states" into the arguments for plot_BioGeoBEARS_results(), wherever it appears in your script.

As you can see in the first script, "mix_colors_for_states" is what mixes the single-area colors into the mixed colors for the (many, many) ranges with multiple areas.

Or, you could just manually specify "colors_list_for_states" as a list of colors, but if you have 350 possible states/ranges, you will have to specify 350 colors.s

Cheers!
Nick

